scripts/upgrade.sh-10-# What it does:
scripts/upgrade.sh-11-#   - Backs up the current .claude/team.md, .claude/frontend-team.md, .claude/skills/,
scripts/upgrade.sh-12-#     .claude/hooks/, .claude/scripts/, .claude/commands/, .claude/pitfalls-catalog.yaml,
scripts/upgrade.sh-13-#     .claude/task-chains.yaml to .claude.bak/{timestamp}/
scripts/upgrade.sh-14-#   - (F-CHAOS-3) Before overwriting any adopter file that differs from the source,
scripts/upgrade.sh-15-#     emits a `diff -q`-style WARNING line (shown on stderr) so the Owner is aware
scripts/upgrade.sh-16-#     a customization will be replaced. Pass --no-diff-warn to silence.
scripts/upgrade.sh-17-#     Pass --skip=<glob> to exclude files from the overwrite entirely (one --skip per pattern).
scripts/upgrade.sh-18-#   - Replaces them with the latest from this repo, respecting --profile and --stack
scripts/upgrade.sh-19-#   - Leaves CLAUDE.md, MEMORY.md, .claude/agent-metrics.md untouched — those are
scripts/upgrade.sh:20:#     user-customized files. .claude/settings.json is preserved as-is for its
scripts/upgrade.sh-21-#     existing keys, but the PLAN-135 W2 settings-merge step (below) ADDITIVELY
scripts/upgrade.sh-22-#     registers new framework lifecycle hooks into it (idempotent, non-clobbering).
scripts/upgrade.sh-23-#   - (DevOps-P1-4) Refreshes the PROTOCOL.md pointer to keep it aligned with the
scripts/upgrade.sh:24:#     current source layout (framework-derived content, not user data).
scripts/upgrade.sh-25-#   - (PLAN-135 W1 w0r) Pre-flight ADVISORY model-deprecation scan of the target
scripts/upgrade.sh-26-#     via .claude/scripts/check-model-deprecations.py when present: already-retired
scripts/upgrade.sh-27-#     or <=60-days-to-retirement Claude model ids emit stderr WARNING lines.
scripts/upgrade.sh-28-#     NEVER blocks the upgrade — any infra failure degrades to a NOTE (fail-open).
scripts/upgrade.sh-29-#     Pass --no-deprecation-warn to silence.
scripts/upgrade.sh-30-#   - (PLAN-135 W2 H8) Idempotent settings-merge step. install.sh EXISTS-SKIPs an
scripts/upgrade.sh-31-#     existing .claude/settings.json, so a fresh-install-only hook registration
scripts/upgrade.sh-32-#     never reaches the S217 population of existing adopters. This step registers
scripts/upgrade.sh-33-#     the new framework lifecycle hooks (today: the `Setup`/`init` post-install
scripts/upgrade.sh-34-#     self-verification hook check_setup_verification.py) into the adopter's
