The night-mode cure has a second, more direct partial-delivery case: both install and upgrade preserve any pre-existing `.claude/.gitignore` wholesale. For `--ceremony user`, the root ignore is deliberately skipped, so an adopter-owned nested ignore that lacks the two new entries leaves the exact original leak intact; the efficacy suite only uses targets where that file is absent. I’m checking whether another delivered ignore source closes that case (so far, none does).
