   125	Do **not** stack them on one repo. Mixing paths produces a known failure mode: hooks registered twice (once in `.claude/settings.json`, once via the plugin's own hook registration), so every governed action pays the hook chain twice; settings merges stacked on top of each other; and a drifted install manifest — the manifest records only the last writer, so `uninstall.sh` can no longer faithfully remove the earlier install and leaves orphans behind.
   126	
   127	If you have mixed paths, recover in this order:
   128	
   129	1. **Uninstall via the path you installed with.** Script or npx installs: `scripts/uninstall.sh <target> --dry-run` first, then for real. The npm shim only exposes the installer, so run `uninstall.sh` from a clone — it honours the same manifest the bundled installer wrote. Plugin: remove it through Claude Code's plugin manager.
   130	2. **Verify `.claude/` is clean.** No `team.md`, `hooks/`, `skills/`, or `.install-manifest.sha256` left behind. The uninstaller deliberately preserves files you modified after install, so inspect and remove leftovers by hand.
   131	3. **Reinstall via exactly one path.**
   132	
   133	See [`INSTALL.md`](INSTALL.md) for the full option-by-option guide.
   134	
   135	By default the installer copies the core and frontend skill profiles and the governance hooks. Select profiles and stack hooks explicitly:
   136	
   137	```bash
   138	./scripts/install.sh /path/to/your-app --profile core,frontend,fintech --stack node
   139	```
   140	
   141	Two install modes:
   142	
   143	- `--ceremony maintainer` (default): full governance, including signed-edit ceremonies on protected paths.
   144	- `--ceremony user`: advisory hooks only, no signing — writes only under `.claude/`. Good for a low-friction trial.
   145	
   146	### Harness: Claude Code (default), Codex CLI, or Grok Build
   147	
   148	The same enforcement hooks run under three harnesses. `--harness claude` (the default; byte-identical to omitting the flag) registers the hooks for Claude Code. `--harness codex` additionally emits a Codex bundle — `.codex/hooks.json`, `.codex/rules/ceo.rules`, and an operator `AGENTS.md` — that invokes the **same** hooks with `CEO_HOOK_ADAPTER=codex`:
   149	
   150	```bash
   151	./scripts/install.sh /path/to/your-app --harness codex
   152	```
   153	
   154	Under Codex the rails are **per-rail**, verified against codex-cli 0.139.0: canonical-edit, bash-safety, plan-lifecycle, kernel-deny, config, and kill-switch are ENFORCED at edit time; the audit chain is ENFORCED but completeness-bounded; the pair-rail is inverted (Codex operates, `claude -p` reviews) and PARTIAL; **spawn governance is ADVISORY, not enforced**. Two things bound every ENFORCED claim: **nothing is enforced until you grant Codex `/hooks` trust** (the installer prints the exact steps and ends with an `ARMED / NOT-ARMED-(untrusted) / BROKEN` arming check), and codex-cli fail-opens on hook death — an untrusted or crashed hook is a silent no-op. See [`docs/adapters.md`](docs/adapters.md), [`docs/provider_capability_matrix.md`](docs/provider_capability_matrix.md), and [`INSTALL.md`](INSTALL.md) `--harness codex`.
   155	
   156	`--harness grok` runs the **same** hooks under xAI Grok Build. Grok reads the framework's legacy-compat `.claude/settings.json` as a Claude-compatible registration, so this is a **single-surface** install — it arms the shipped `.claude/settings.json` (no `.grok/hooks/` bundle; arming both surfaces would double-fire every hook) and emits `AGENTS.md`, `.grok/*.example` config, and a git pre-push review gate:
   157	
   158	```bash
   159	./scripts/install.sh /path/to/your-app --harness grok
   160	```
   161	
   162	Verified against grok 0.2.93 (an **exact** pin, not a range — Grok Build ships 1–2 releases/day). The prevention rails (canonical-edit, bash-safety on grok's native `run_terminal_command`, plan-lifecycle, kernel-deny, `.grok` kill-switch) are ENFORCED at edit time via grok's only blocking event, `pre_tool_use`; the audit chain is ENFORCED but completeness-bounded; **spawn governance is ADVISORY** (SubagentStart is passive). The pair-rail is inverted and **Stop-passive** — grok's Stop hook cannot force the review, so the **git pre-push gate is the teeth**. As with Codex, two things bound every ENFORCED claim: nothing fires until you grant Grok **folder trust** (`grok --trust`, unified across MCP/LSP/hooks), and grok fail-opens on hook death (crash / timeout / malformed = silent allow). Separately, `/council <scope>` runs an ADVISORY cross-vendor audit (Claude + Codex + Grok), fail-loud and never in CI. See [`docs/adapters.md`](docs/adapters.md) and [`INSTALL.md`](INSTALL.md) `--harness grok`.
   163	
   164	To verify the safety guards actually block what they claim, run the in-process self-test (hermetic, no network, no cost):
   165	
   166	```bash
   167	# from inside your installed project, in Claude Code
   168	/self-test
   169	```
   170	
   171	To remove the framework cleanly:
   172	
   173	```bash
   174	/path/to/ceo-orchestration/scripts/uninstall.sh /path/to/your-app
   175	```
   176	
   177	---
   178	
   179	## Verifying the numbers
   180	
    40	      `INSTALL.md` (`--pin vX.Y.Z`) ·
    41	      `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` (`currently vX.Y.Z, aligned with the repo`) ·
    42	      `npm/README.md` (`last-reviewed: <data> vX.Y.Z`) ·
    43	      `npm/package.json` (`"version"`) · `pyproject.toml` (`version =`) ·
    44	      `SBOM.md` (`**Version:** \`X.Y.Z\``) ·
    45	      `.claude/.framework-version` (marker que o updater dos adopters lê
    46	      MARKER-FIRST; reescrito pelo bump driver — site real em
    47	      `_release_bump_sites.py`) ·
    48	      `SECURITY.md` + `VERSIONING.md` (janela de suporte
    49	      `Current/Previous MINOR (vX.Y.x)` — **família minor**).
    50	      O **shift da janela de suporte** (`Previous` ← `Current`) é COBERTO
    51	      pelo driver em bump de MINOR (kinds `minor`/`prev_minor` em
    52	      `_release_bump_sites.py`, derivados do target com a MESMA regra do
    53	      oráculo: prev = minor−1) — a exceção é target `X.0.0`, onde o
    54	      `Previous` não é derivável: o driver o deixa intacto e AVISA alto
    55	      ("release-train judgment"), e o `verify-counts` também não
    56	      value-checka prev em X.0. ⚠ A **anotação da tag** segue MANUAL de
    57	      propósito — a prosa da tag **nenhum gate prova**, então releia-a
    58	      antes de assinar.
    59	      **`CLAUDE.md` e `README.md` NÃO são sites de versão** — nunca
    60	      carregaram literal de versão (`git log -S 'VERSION='` não acha
    61	      commit que o tenha adicionado); procurá-los num bump é perder tempo
    62	      atrás de literal inexistente
    63	      **+ os 2 manifests de plugin** (`.claude-plugin/{plugin,marketplace}.json`,
    64	      regenerados via `scripts/build-plugin.py --write-manifests`, nunca
    65	      hand-patch; o gate deles vive só no `release.yml`).
    66	      O badge do README **não** é site de versão — é dinâmico e o driver
    67	      não o toca; auditar por ele deixa passar drift real.
    68	      O driver cobre TODOS os sites mecânicos **enumerados acima**, janela
    69	      de suporte incluída — **exceto** a prosa da tag, manual por desenho
    70	      (ver o aviso acima e §Promote stable), e o `Previous MINOR` num
    71	      target `X.0.0` (avisado alto, nunca adivinhado). Leia isso como
    72	      cobertura sobre a **lista**, não sobre o repositório: um literal de
    73	      versão que exista fora da lista não é bump-eável e simplesmente não
    74	      deveria existir. Quem responde pela **exaustividade sobre o repo** é
    75	      o scanner de superfícies vivas
    76	      (`SCAN_ROOTS` em `.claude/scripts/tests/test_release_bump_sites.py`,
    77	      hoje `.github/`, `RELEASE.md`, `.claude/scripts/`, `scripts/`,
    78	      `npm/INTEGRITY.md` e `npm/README.md`) — foi a ausência dos docs de
    79	      `npm/` ali que deixou `npm/INTEGRITY.md` declarar uma versão obsoleta
    80	      sem que nenhum gate visse (PLAN-177 P1-2). Note que as duas entradas
    81	      de `npm/` são **arquivos**, não a pasta: `npm/` recebe, no staging do
    82	      publish e num build local, uma cópia espelhada de `.claude/**` +
    83	      `scripts/**`, e varrer a pasta faria o scanner auditar clones do
    84	      próprio repo. Superfície nova que possa carregar versão entra no
    85	      `SCAN_ROOTS` **antes** de entrar no release.
    86	
    87	### Governança
    88	
    89	- [ ] Branch protection `main` ativo no GitHub
    90	- [ ] CODEOWNERS cobre `.claude/team.md`, skills core, ADRs
    91	- [ ] Chave GPG de release do Owner disponível (`gpg -K`).
    92	      `commit.gpgsign`/`tag.gpgsign` ficam **UNSET por design** — commits
    93	      comuns não são assinados; o driver assina a TAG inline com `-u`
    94	      (o que o Owner assina no release é a tag, não os commits)
    95	- [ ] Todos os ADRs novos têm Status: ACCEPTED
    96	
    97	### Hooks sanity
    98	
    99	- [ ] Hook `check_agent_spawn.py` bloqueia spawn sem SKILL
   100	- [ ] Hook `check_bash_safety.py` bloqueia `rm -rf`
README.md:98:> **Official sources only.** The only official distribution points are the GitHub repository [`Canhada-Labs/ceo-orchestration`](https://github.com/Canhada-Labs/ceo-orchestration) and the npm package [`ceo-orchestration`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/ceo-orchestration) (`npx ceo-orchestration`). Any other mirror, fork, re-published package, marketplace listing, or lookalike name is unofficial and untrusted. GitHub releases ship a SHA-256 checksum for `install.sh` (that is the whole checksum coverage — see `SECURITY.md` §How to verify what you install) and the npm package is published with SLSA **Level 2** provenance (`npm publish --provenance`; Level 3 is out of scope) — verify before installing.
