    18	are explicit (never silent): a malformed payload returns a payload with
    19	`raw_error` set so the caller can decide whether to fail-open or block.
    20	
    21	## Safety properties
    22	
    23	1. Reads stdin exactly once (subsequent calls return empty; matches the
    24	   bash `INPUT=$(cat)` pattern).
    25	2. Tolerates missing fields (all fields default to empty string / empty dict).
    26	3. Never raises on bad JSON — sets `raw_error` instead.
    27	4. No network, no file I/O, no subprocess.
