     1	# W1 staged pack (v2) — NOTES
     2	
     3	Base: canonical `ba19bcc` (W0 already landed). All work in throwaway clones
     4	under this directory; the canonical repo was never written to.
     5	
     6	The canonical HEAD advanced to `7c09544` (docs-only, the W2 runbook) while this
     7	pack was being built. Re-checked rather than assumed: all nine patches
     8	`git apply --check` clean at `7c09544`, individually and combined, on a fresh
     9	clone. No rebase needed.
    10	
    11	This is the **v2** of the pack. It starts from the v1/v4 drafts under
    12	`../w1-staged/` and `../w1v4/`, rebases them onto `ba19bcc`, **re-runs every
    13	verification from scratch** (nothing here is inherited as a claim), and closes
    14	the gaps the mandate named. Deltas are listed in §7.
    15	
    16	## 1. Patches — 9, one per surface
    17	
    18	| patch | surface | canonicality | change |
    19	|---|---|---|---|
    20	| `w1-generator.patch` | `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh` | **CANONICAL** | +6 functions (the ONE text) |
    21	| `w1-install.patch` | `scripts/install.sh` | **CANONICAL** | 2 delegations + new delivery |
    22	| `w1-upgrade.patch` | `scripts/upgrade.sh` | **CANONICAL** | 2 new delivery blocks |
    23	| `w1-install-npm.patch` | `scripts/install-npm.sh` | **CANONICAL** | comment block `:176-190` |
    24	| `w1-tournament.patch` | `.github/workflows/tournament.yml` | **CANONICAL** | T-1 `working-directory` |
    25	| `w1-smoke-install-wiring.patch` | `.github/workflows/smoke-install.yml` | **CANONICAL** | 2 path filters + step + timeout 25→32 |
    26	| `w1-parity-allowlist.patch` | `scripts/tests/_parity_classify.py` | free | −10 (the allowlist tuple) |
    27	| `w1-nightmode-e2e.patch` | `scripts/tests/test-night-mode-ignore-effect.sh` | free | new file, **mode 100755** |
    28	| `w1-tournament-assert.patch` | `.claude/scripts/tests/test_tournament_projection_workdir.py` | free | new file |
    29	
    30	All nine `git apply --check` clean **individually and as one invocation**
    31	against a fresh clone of the canonical repo; applied there, the resulting
    32	`git diff` is byte-identical to the working clone's (`cmp` — empty).
    33	Any order applies (nine hunks in nine files). They must land in ONE commit —
    34	§4.
    35	
    36	**`w1-claude-gitignore.patch` was NOT emitted, deliberately.** The mandate asks
    37	for it "se separável" and it is not: the `.claude/.gitignore` body lives in the
    38	same generator file as the other two blocks, and its delivery is a hunk inside
    39	each of `install.sh` / `upgrade.sh`. Splitting it out means hand-editing three
    40	`.patch` files, which this repo has a rule against for exactly this reason. It
    41	is delivered by `w1-generator` + `w1-install` + `w1-upgrade`.
    42	
    43	## 2. Sentinel scope — measured, not recalled
    44	
    45	The commit touches **nine** paths. The sentinel `## Scope` must enumerate all
    46	of them, including the three free ones, or `touched − scope = ∅` fails:
    47	
    48	    scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh                              CANONICAL
    49	    scripts/install.sh                                              CANONICAL
    50	    scripts/upgrade.sh                                              CANONICAL
    51	    scripts/install-npm.sh                                          CANONICAL
    52	    .github/workflows/tournament.yml                                CANONICAL
    53	    .github/workflows/smoke-install.yml                             CANONICAL
    54	    scripts/tests/_parity_classify.py                               free
    55	    scripts/tests/test-night-mode-ignore-effect.sh                  free (mode 100755)
    56	    .claude/scripts/tests/test_tournament_projection_workdir.py     free
    57	
    58	Produced by calling `check_canonical_edit._is_canonical(path, Path(repo))` on
    59	each path, with a positive control (`.claude/team.md` → CANONICAL) and a
    60	negative one (`README.md` → free). Passing `repo_root` as a **`str`** makes
    61	every path come back "free" — a silent wrong answer that would yield a sentinel
    62	scope missing every canonical file. Worth repeating if anyone re-derives this.
    63	
    64	**Preserve the exec bit** on `test-night-mode-ignore-effect.sh`: the patch
    65	carries `new file mode 100755`, but a `cp`-based land drops it (the verified
    66	S286 failure mode).
    67	
    68	## 3. CF-9 — the generator owns every .gitignore surface
    69	
    70	`_framework_manifest_set.sh` gains six functions after the
    71	`_render_protocol_pointer` family:
    72	
    73	* `_mcp_secrets_ignore_entry` / `_apply_mcp_secrets_ignore` — PLAN-019 P2-SEC-H
    74	  block (`state/mcp_client_secrets/`), create-or-append.
    75	* `_posture_state_ignore_entries` / `_apply_posture_state_ignores` — PLAN-165
    76	  CX-3 block, append-only.
    77	* `_claude_dir_gitignore_body` / `_apply_claude_dir_gitignore` — the new file.
    78	
    79	Owning only the posture block would leave the mcp-secrets block as a second
    80	unowned copy of the same kind of text on the same file — a ceremony granting
    81	ownership of half a surface — and would leave the pre-v1.2.0 adopter, who never
    82	got the secrets entry from an upgrade either.
    83	
    84	House style followed exactly: no `local`, no `[[ ]]`, `_prefix_`-scoped
    85	globals, POSIX test (the file declares itself bash-3.2-safe and contains zero
    86	`local` and zero `[[`).
    87	
    88	**Two byte-level idiosyncrasies are preserved deliberately**, and the generator
    89	says so in a comment: (1) the posture header comment is emitted *inside* the
    90	loop, once per appended entry; (2) the mcp CREATE branch writes its header with
    91	**no** leading blank line while the APPEND branch writes one. Both are planted
    92	as mutations in `BYTE-PROOF.md` §F and the harness goes red on each.
    93	
    94	### `.claude/.gitignore` — the new delivered file
    95	
    96	Body: provenance header + `/state/` + `/settings.local.json`, leading-slash
    97	anchored so they bind to `.claude/` only.
    98	
    99	* Delivered in **every** ceremony on **both** routes. It lives inside
   100	  `.claude/`, so it does not violate the `--ceremony user` invariant — asserted
   101	  by the e2e's scenario C, which runs the exact top-level check
   102	  `smoke-install.yml:220-232` performs and finds only `.claude` and `.git`.
   103	* **Create-if-missing, never rewritten.** `BYTE-PROOF.md` §D writes an adopter
   104	  edit into it and re-runs the upgrade block: preserved byte-for-byte.
   105	* **Not in the baseline manifest, by construction** — so no later upgrade can
   106	  classify it as framework-owned and clobber it. Verified on a REAL install:
   107	  `grep -c gitignore <target>/.claude/.install-manifest.sha256` → **0**, while
   108	  the install-state journal carries all three ops
   109	  (`ensure_mcp_secrets_dir`, `ensure_posture_state_ignores`,
   110	  `ensure_claude_dir_gitignore`, one each).
   111	* `uninstall.sh` only removes manifest-listed files, so it leaves this file
   112	  alone. Verified: `uninstall.sh --dry-run` on that target →
   113	  `grep -ci gitignore` = **0**, 513 removals, none of them a `.gitignore`.
   114	
   115	### The two new test files do not reach the npm tarball
   116	
   117	Both live under a `tests/` directory, and the npm packlist gate
   118	(`validate.yml:1030-1069`) stages with `--exclude='**/tests/'` over the same
   119	`for src in scripts templates .claude …` loop that would otherwise carry them.
   120	So `scripts/tests/test-night-mode-ignore-effect.sh` and
   121	`.claude/scripts/tests/test_tournament_projection_workdir.py` are excluded by
   122	the existing rule — no packlist change needed, and none was made. Read from the
   123	workflow, not assumed.
   124	
   125	## 4. Atomicity (why ONE commit) — and why a human has to check it
   126	
   127	The allowlist removal and the upgrade delivery are two halves of one change:
   128	
   129	* allowlist removed **without** the upgrade cure ⇒ the gate goes FATAL
   130	  (measured: `STATE-D-PROOF.md`).
   131	* upgrade cure **without** the allowlist removal ⇒ the gate keeps allowlisting a
   132	  defect that no longer exists.
   133	
   134	Nothing enforces this. The `^\.gitignore$` tuple lives in `ACCEPTED`, not
   135	`KNOWN_OPEN`, and only `KNOWN_OPEN` entries are MANDATORY-FIRE; an orphan
   136	`ACCEPTED` entry is a WARNING. `git show --stat` before the push is the check.
   137	
   138	## 5. Deliberate posture, stated so it is a decision and not a surprise
   139	
   140	Idempotence is **per line** (`grep -Fxq`), not per block. An adopter who
   141	deliberately deletes one entry gets it re-appended on the next install/upgrade,
   142	with a fresh header comment. That is intentional — these entries keep secrets
   143	and per-machine permission posture out of VCS, and the framework cannot
   144	distinguish a deliberate deletion from an accident. `BYTE-PROOF.md` §E asserts
   145	the re-append so a future change to this posture is a visible test failure
   146	rather than silent drift. An adopter who really wants the path tracked should
   147	use `.git/info/exclude` or a nested `.gitignore`. Release notes should say so.
   148	
   149	The root `.gitignore` blocks also survive `uninstall.sh` (it removes only
   150	manifest-listed files, and the adopter's `.gitignore` is not one). That was
   151	already true of the mcp block before this change; it is not new, and it is the
   152	safe direction.
   153	
   154	## 6. Fail-loud on a missing generator
   155	
   156	`install.sh` guards each call with `command -v … || { echo "    ERROR: …" >&2;
   157	return 1; }` in the literal shape of `install.sh:1898`; under `set -e` that
   158	aborts the install. `upgrade.sh` cannot `return` at top level, so it `exit 1`s.
   159	
   160	That is install.sh's posture for this library, NOT the preserve-the-surface
   161	posture of `_refresh_protocol_pointer`: nothing here overwrites an adopter
   162	file, the operation is a pure append, so there is no surface a silent degrade
   163	would be protecting. It does abort an upgrade at ~95% completion (before the
   164	baseline-manifest rewrite) — worth an explicit Owner look. The alternative,
   165	warn-and-continue, would reinstate silent non-delivery, which is the P1 class
   166	itself.
   167	
   168	## 7. What v2 changed relative to the v1/v4 drafts
   169	
   170	1. **Rebased and re-verified at `ba19bcc`.** Every run in `PARITY-RUN.md`,
   171	   `BYTE-PROOF.md` and `STATE-D-PROOF.md` is a fresh execution at this base;
   172	   no result was carried over.
   173	2. **`install-npm.sh`: a new half-false claim removed.** The v4 draft replaced
   174	   the impossible consumer recipe with "a maintainer can re-verify a locally
   175	   built artifact with `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt` from NPM_DIR". Measured:
   176	   that also fails. `npm/*.tgz` is git-ignored, the manifest keeps one line per
   177	   tarball NAME across versions, and a bulk check therefore exits **1** with
   178	   `ceo-orchestration-1.0.0.tgz: FAILED open or read` (reproduced with the
   179	   repo's own tracked manifest plus a freshly built tarball). The comment now
   180	   says which of the two artifacts actually verifies — the per-tarball
   181	   `<tarball>.sha256` sidecar, measured rc=0 — and why the cumulative manifest
   182	   does not. Curing a false promise with a slightly less false promise is the
   183	   class this P1 is about.
   184	   The forbidden literal `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt` (blocked in
   185	   `npm/INTEGRITY.md` by the landed
   186	   `test_integrity_doc_makes_no_enforced_claim_for_the_tarball_checksum`)
   187	   survives in the pack in exactly one place — the REMOVAL side of
   188	   `w1-install-npm.patch` (`-#   sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt`, one line, with a
   189	   `-` sign). In the resulting tree it is gone: `grep -rn` over
   190	   `scripts/ npm/ .github/ docs/` in the patched clone returns **0** hits.
   191	3. **BYTE-PROOF §A/§B: new scenario `s9_adopter_edited_comment`** — the adopter
   192	   kept the entries but rewrote the header comments the framework appended. The
   193	   mandate named this case; `grep -Fxq` keys on the ENTRY, so nothing may be
   194	   re-appended. Verified: comments preserved, zero framework headers
   195	   re-introduced, entry counts 1/1/1.
   196	4. **BYTE-PROOF §E2 (new): idempotence on the INSTALL route and across routes.**
   197	   v1/v4 tested `upgrade` twice only. Now: install ×2 then upgrade, over four
   198	   scenarios — no-op after the first, counts 1/1/1.
   199	5. **Night-mode e2e: the root block is measured directly, BEFORE and AFTER.**
   200	   `.claude/.gitignore` alone makes every scenario report "clean", and
   201	   `git check-ignore` reports only the winning rule — so an upgrade whose root
   202	   delivery silently did nothing would have passed the v4 test. Scenario A now
   203	   asserts posture entries go `0 → 2` across the upgrade (and scaffold-errors if
   204	   the pin ever stops reproducing the gap: `git show v1.2.0:scripts/install.sh
