     6	## Why a human has to see this red
     7	
     8	The `.gitignore` tuple this pack deletes lives in `ACCEPTED`, **not** in
     9	`KNOWN_OPEN`. Only `KNOWN_OPEN` entries are MANDATORY-FIRE (an entry that
    10	matches nothing is fatal — "the bug you named is closed, delete the entry").
    11	An orphan `ACCEPTED` entry is a WARNING, printed and survivable. So nothing in
    12	CI would have complained if the allowlist removal had landed *without* the
    13	upgrade delivery, or the delivery *without* the removal. The atomicity of CF-2
    14	is enforced by this proof and by landing both in one commit — not by a gate.
